course: dictionary
lesson: 8154
title: Rescue: saving someone from danger
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To rescue someone or something is to save them from danger, harm or a bad situation. «Nine-year-old Ella Brown rescued six ducklings from a drain on Monday.» The ducklings were in danger in the drain, and Ella saved them from it.
explain: As a noun, a rescue is the act of saving someone. In safety work, rescues are done by trained people such as lifeguards, firefighters and coastguards. If you see someone in trouble, your job is to get help, not to be the rescuer yourself.
explain: Rescue also appears in useful phrases: come to the rescue, rescue team, rescue dog, sea rescue, mountain rescue and rescue someone from. A rescue animal is a pet taken in from a shelter after being lost, hurt or unwanted. Context tells you which meaning is being used.
fact: To rescue means to save someone or something from danger or harm.
fact: As a noun, a rescue is the act of saving someone.
fact: «Reach or throw, don't go»: if someone is in trouble in water, do not jump in; shout for help, call the emergency number and throw something that floats.
fact: «A seal pup alone on a beach is usually not lost», so keep away and call a rescue group.
fact: «Rescue centres take in lost or given-up animals», and many older animals are already trained and calm.
exercise: «Nine-year-old Ella Brown rescued six ducklings from a drain on Monday.» What does rescued mean here? | Counted carefully | *Saved from danger | Fed at a park | Moved to a new town
exercise: «If someone is in trouble in water, do not jump in.» What should you do instead? | Wait on the sand until they swim to shore alone | Jump in quickly and swim out to them | *Shout for help and throw something that floats
exercise: What is a rescue dog? | A dog that only lives on a farm | A dog that wins prizes at shows | *A pet taken in from a shelter after being lost, hurt or unwanted
test: «A seal pup alone on a beach is usually not lost.» Why should you keep away from it? | Seals are not allowed on beaches | *Its mother may be fishing nearby | It is always lost and needs taking home
test: «If you find an injured wild bird, tell an adult who can call a wildlife rescue.» What is the best thing to do? | Take it home and feed it bread | *Tell an adult who can call a wildlife rescue | Wait for it to fly away on its own
exam: Which phrase means a team trained to save people who are lost or hurt in the hills? | *mountain rescue | rescue someone from | sea rescue | rescue dog
